  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Using the relation between the range of the radio communication and the height of the transmission antenna&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></math> and the receiving antenna&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></math>, the maximum line of sight distance between two antennas, is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>80</mn></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>=</mo><mn>64000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math></p>"
